# Files that are consumed by Linux must keep LF endings regardless of the
# platform they were authored on. A shell script checked out with CRLF fails
# on the VPS with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, and systemd silently
# mis-parses unit files whose lines end in \r.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf
